  "summary": "S2 to S5 adopted after S1. Target artifacts carry the lab's interpretation metadata; the lab registry keeps workloads and five retired definitions. admitArtifact admits each artifact once as current, stale or unknown from its receipt, its recipe and the inputs its producer recorded; only current rows read ok or count as coverage, and threshold rows claim only operator-independent verdicts. Target history and report show each target's latest run and recipe state; health, the viewer and the landing index show admission. One S5 evaluator assesses matrices under s5-no-regression-v1 and s5-work-gain-profile120-v1, with correctness bound to a per-cell, per-arm preflight and the served build id. The code-block clock starts before the editor's handlers, external-text samples are dense and copied, and seven strict producers write measurements before validating. The lab READMEs teach the flow, and the pinned Evidence Kit CLI reads the adapted rows.",
